---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Amiga – Learn AMOS Professional and Master the Custom Chipset"
  description="Learn Amiga programming from AMOS Professional to 68000 assembly. Master the custom chipset (Agnus, Denise, Paula, Gary), blitter operations, and copper effects. Tier 1 beginning now."
>
  <style>
    .system-hero {
      min-height: 400px;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff6600 0%, #cc5200 100%);
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      position: relative;
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    .system-hero::before {
      content: '';
      position: absolute;
      top: 0;
      left: 0;
      right: 0;
      bottom: 0;
      background-image:
        repeating-linear-gradient(
          0deg,
          transparent,
          transparent 2px,
          rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1) 2px,
          rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1) 4px
        );
      pointer-events: none;
    }

    .hero-content {
      text-align: center;
      color: white;
      padding: var(--space-8) var(--space-4);
      position: relative;
      z-index: 1;
      max-width: 800px;
    }

    .system-title {
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
      font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
      font-weight: 900;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
      text-shadow: 2px 2px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
    }

    .system-subtitle {
      font-size: 1.5rem;
      opacity: 0.95;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    }

    .system-specs {
      display: flex;
      gap: var(--space-8);
      justify-content: center;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      margin-top: var(--space-6);
    }

    .spec-item {
      text-align: center;
    }

    .spec-label {
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      opacity: 0.8;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    }

    .spec-value {
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      font-weight: bold;
    }

    .content-section {
      padding: var(--space-16) var(--space-4);
      max-width: 1200px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .section-title {
      font-size: 2rem;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
      color: var(--color-text);
    }

    .feature-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));
      gap: var(--space-6);
      margin-top: var(--space-8);
    }

    .feature-card {
      background: var(--color-surface);
      border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
      border-radius: 0.5rem;
      padding: var(--space-6);
    }

    .feature-title {
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      color: #ff6600;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    }

    .feature-description {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    .chipset-map {
      background: var(--color-surface);
      border: 2px solid #ff6600;
      border-radius: 0.5rem;
      padding: var(--space-6);
      margin: var(--space-8) 0;
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
    }

    .chipset-item {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      padding: var(--space-2) 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    }

    .chipset-item:last-child {
      border-bottom: none;
    }

    .chipset-name {
      color: #ff6600;
      font-weight: bold;
    }

    .chipset-description {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    }

    .status-strip {
      background: var(--color-surface);
      border: 2px solid #ff6600;
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
      padding: var(--space-4);
      margin: var(--space-6) auto 0;
      max-width: 720px;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .status-strip a {
      color: #ff6600;
      font-weight: 700;
      text-decoration: none;
      border-bottom: 1px solid #ff660040;
      padding-bottom: 2px;
    }

    .status-strip small {
      display: block;
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      margin-top: var(--space-2);
    }

    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      .system-specs {
        gap: var(--space-4);
      }

      .feature-grid {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }
    }
  </style>

  <!-- System Hero -->
  <section class="system-hero">
    <div class="hero-content">
      <h1 class="system-title">AMIGA</h1>
      <p class="system-subtitle">Custom chipset power meets structured BASIC</p>
      <p style="font-style: italic; opacity: 0.9;">The ultimate 16-bit games machine. Tier 1 beginning now.</p>
      <div class="system-specs">
        <div class="spec-item">
          <div class="spec-label">CPU</div>
          <div class="spec-value">MC68000</div>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-item">
          <div class="spec-label">Speed</div>
          <div class="spec-value">7.16 MHz</div>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-item">
          <div class="spec-label">RAM</div>
          <div class="spec-value">512 KB+</div>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-item">
          <div class="spec-label">Released</div>
          <div class="spec-value">1985</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="status-strip">
    <div><a href="/commodore-amiga/game-01-hop/unit-01">Unit 01: The Lanes</a> is live.</div>
    <small>Units 02–08 coming soon.</small>
  </div>

  <!-- Course Paths -->
  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Learning Paths</h2>

    <div class="feature-grid" style="margin-top: var(--space-6);">
      <div class="feature-card" style="border: 2px solid #ff6600;">
        <h3 class="feature-title">📘 AMOS Professional</h3>
        <p class="feature-description" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-4);">
          Start with AMOS Professional — a game-focused BASIC designed specifically for the Amiga's custom chipset.
          Built-in sprite and music editors, structured programming, and direct access to the blitter, copper, and Paula.
          Master Screen Open, multiple layered displays, bitplanes, and proportional fonts.
        </p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: var(--space-3);"><strong>Tier 1 Complete • 16 lessons available</strong></p>
        <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: 0.9rem;">
          <li>✅ Tier 1: Discovery — Screen Open, Lowres/Hires/HAM modes, colour palettes, bitplanes, Curs Off, Cls, Ink, Centre, Locate commands, sprite basics, complete mini action game — Complete!</li>
          <li style="margin-top: var(--space-3);">→ 16 comprehensive lessons from first Screen Open to complete synthesis game</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/commodore-amiga/phase-0"
           style="display: inline-block; margin-top: var(--space-4); padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-4);
                  background: #ff6600; color: white; border-radius: 0.375rem;
                  text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.9rem;">
          Start Learning AMOS →
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-card" style="border: 2px solid var(--color-border); opacity: 0.7;">
        <h3 class="feature-title">⚙️ 68000 Assembly</h3>
        <p class="feature-description" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-4);">
          Master 68000 assembly programming. Direct hardware control of Agnus (blitter), Denise (video), Paula (sound),
          and Gary (memory). Learn the architecture that powered not just the Amiga, but the Atari ST, Sega Genesis,
          and early Macintosh.
        </p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: var(--space-3);"><strong>Coming soon: Phase 1 begins with foundations</strong></p>
        <div style="display: inline-block; margin-top: var(--space-4); padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-4);
                    background: var(--color-surface); color: var(--color-text-secondary); border: 2px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 0.375rem;
                    font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.9rem;">
          In Development
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What You'll Learn -->
  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">What You'll Learn</h2>

    <div class="feature-grid">
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3 class="feature-title">Custom Chipset</h3>
        <p class="feature-description">
          Master Agnus (blitter + copper), Denise (video), Paula (sound + disk), and Gary (memory management).
          The Amiga's custom chips give you hardware acceleration for graphics, sound, and I/O.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3 class="feature-title">Blitter Operations</h3>
        <p class="feature-description">
          Learn hardware-accelerated graphics via the blitter. Copy, fill, and combine bitmaps at hardware speed.
          Understand DMA, channels, and how the Amiga achieves smooth scrolling and sprite movement.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3 class="feature-title">Copper Programming</h3>
        <p class="feature-description">
          Program the copper (co-processor) to change colours mid-frame, create gradient skies, and achieve
          effects impossible on other machines. The copper runs in parallel with the CPU.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3 class="feature-title">Paula Sound</h3>
        <p class="feature-description">
          4-channel 8-bit PCM audio at 28 kHz. Mix samples, create tracker music, and achieve sound quality
          that made the Amiga legendary. Paula handles sound independently while you focus on gameplay.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3 class="feature-title">Multiple Screens</h3>
        <p class="feature-description">
          Layer up to 8 independent screens with different resolutions, colours, and bitplanes. The Amiga's
          display architecture lets you create complex UIs and effects other machines can't match.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Development Environment -->
  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Development Environment</h2>
    <p style="color: var(--color-text-secondary); margin-bottom: var(--space-6); max-width: 800px;">
      Program the Amiga using FS-UAE or WinUAE emulators with cycle-accurate hardware emulation. Boot Workbench,
      load AMOS Professional, and start coding with the built-in sprite and music editors. Or dive into 68000
      assembly with vasm cross-development.
    </p>

    <div class="feature-grid">
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3 class="feature-title">🎮 FS-UAE / WinUAE</h3>
        <p class="feature-description">
          Cycle-accurate Amiga emulation supporting all models from A500 to A4000. Save states, ADF disk images,
          and WHDLoad support for instant game loading.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3 class="feature-title">📝 AMOS Professional</h3>
        <p class="feature-description">
          Integrated development environment with sprite editor, music composer, and resource banks. Edit graphics
          and sound while your program is paused, then continue coding.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3 class="feature-title">🛠️ Cross Development</h3>
        <p class="feature-description">
          For assembly: use vasm to cross-compile 68000 code, generate ADF images, and test in FS-UAE. Modern
          workflow with vintage results.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3 class="feature-title">💾 ADF Disk Images</h3>
        <p class="feature-description">
          Work with standard Amiga Disk Format images. Create, modify, and share your programs. Run them on
          real hardware via Gotek floppy emulators.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Custom Chipset Overview -->
  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Amiga Custom Chipset</h2>
    <p style="color: var(--color-text-secondary); max-width: 800px; margin-bottom: var(--space-6);">
      The Amiga's custom chips work in parallel, giving you hardware-accelerated graphics, sound, and I/O.
      This is what made the Amiga the ultimate games machine.
    </p>

    <div class="chipset-map">
      <div class="chipset-item">
        <span class="chipset-name">Agnus</span>
        <span class="chipset-description">Blitter + Copper + DMA controller</span>
      </div>
      <div class="chipset-item">
        <span class="chipset-name">Denise</span>
        <span class="chipset-description">Video processing + sprites + playfields</span>
      </div>
      <div class="chipset-item">
        <span class="chipset-name">Paula</span>
        <span class="chipset-description">4-channel audio + disk + serial I/O</span>
      </div>
      <div class="chipset-item">
        <span class="chipset-name">Gary</span>
        <span class="chipset-description">Memory management + chip select</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Call to Action -->
  <section class="content-section" style="text-align: center;">
    <h2 class="section-title">Ready to Code Like It's 1985?</h2>
    <p style="color: var(--color-text-secondary); margin-bottom: var(--space-6); max-width: 600px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;">
      Boot Workbench, load AMOS Professional, and harness the power of the custom chipset. The Amiga gave
      bedroom coders hardware acceleration—use it to create games that were impossible on other machines.
    </p>
    <div style="display: flex; gap: var(--space-4); justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap;">
      <a href="/commodore-amiga/phase-0"
         style="display: inline-block; padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-6);
                background: #ff6600; color: white; border-radius: 0.5rem;
                text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600;">
        Start Coding →
      </a>
      <a href="https://github.com/code198x"
         style="display: inline-block; padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-6);
                background: transparent; color: #ff6600; border: 2px solid #ff6600; border-radius: 0.5rem;
                text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600;">
        View on GitHub
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
